# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback: without a 404.html, unknown paths serve the app shell.
#
# This built-in behavior makes client-side deep links work. Missing build assets are listed in
# public/_routes.json so functions/[[path]].js intercepts those paths and answers 404 with no-store;
# otherwise a missing chunk could receive the app shell and be cached under the chunk's URL.
#
# Verify with a request
# for any absent asset:
#   curl -sI https://app.dfx.swiss/static/js/999.deadbeef.chunk.js  -> 404
#
# /app2 without a trailing slash would otherwise use the SPA fallback and serve the main app shell
# instead of App2, so this redirect must come before the App 2.0 return-path rules.
# /app2/ and /app2/index.html stay out of _routes.json include (see public/_headers): the
# Function would 404 the App2 shell itself if they were listed.
/app2    /app2/    308
# App 2.0 is hash-routed. Checkout.com and e-mail callbacks hit real paths under
# /app2/.... A 200 rewrite to index.html would keep the nested document URL, so
# relative ./static/js bundles would resolve under /app2/buy/... — redirect into
# the hash under /app2/ instead (query is preserved).
/app2/buy/success    /app2/#/buy/success    302
/app2/buy/success/   /app2/#/buy/success    302
/app2/buy/failure    /app2/#/buy/failure    302
/app2/buy/failure/   /app2/#/buy/failure    302
/app2/account-merge  /app2/#/account-merge  302
/app2/account-merge/ /app2/#/account-merge  302
